# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must use LF regardless of the platform they are
# edited on. A CRLF shebang makes `exec` fail with a bare
# "no such file or directory", which is one of the least helpful errors Linux
# produces — the file is right there, it is the trailing \r that is missing.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf

# Binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
